+ * (n + len) is checked against the cluster limit and the received window
+ * before memmove; this also proves that the n-byte pad follows the header.
+ * The pad is already included in the MPDU length. The caller then uses
+ * iwx_m_adj(m, n) to trim it from the head, so b_wptr remains unchanged and
+ * the derived length decreases by n. Extending b_wptr would expose bytes
+ * beyond the received MPDU as payload.
  *
- * Returns B_FALSE with the buffer untouched if the shift does not fit.
+ * Returns B_FALSE with the buffer untouched if the shift or pad does not fit.
  */
 extern boolean_t iwx_m_shift_right(mblk_t *m, size_t len, size_t n);
 
